{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzBscnvCDEr18V154rJ8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's not clearly a leftover, but SETUP.md doesn't say why it's there.\n\n**What it does:** `kiln/timeparse.py:3` says `KILN_LEGACY_TZ=1` makes `parse()` read timestamps with no timezone as UTC, the way kiln did before 2.0. Without it, those timestamps are read as local time. Nothing else in the repo reads the variable.\n\n**Whether step 4 needs it:** I can't tell from what's here.\n- The tests pass without it (3 run, OK). That doesn't prove much, though. None of them check the timezone `parse()` assigns to a timestamp without one. On a machine set to UTC, which this one probably is, the two modes give the same answer anyway.\n- It has been in SETUP.md since the initial commit (d274cef), and neither that commit nor the doc gives a reason.\n\nSo my guess is that it pins the tests to the old UTC behaviour so results don't depend on the machine's timezone. But that's a guess, and it could equally be left over from before 2.0. If you know it's no longer needed, I can remove it from step 4. Otherwise it's worth asking whoever wrote the setup steps, or running the tests with `TZ` set to a non-UTC zone, both with and without the variable. I haven't changed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":21294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-37>","timestamp":"2026-11-13T03:06:26.436Z","request_id":"req_011CgzBsca2DNyuFmPiFiZxQ"}
